# Build context exclusions for deploy/cloudflare/container.
#
# The context is the repository root, because the Dockerfile copies go-service/.
# That makes this file load-bearing rather than cosmetic: anything not excluded
# here is a candidate for being copied into a layer, and a layer is published to a
# registry. A .env or a rendered wrangler.toml inside this context is a secret in
# an image that anyone with pull access can read, and images are copied, cached
# and pushed far more freely than files in a repository are.

# The plan names this exclusion first for a reason: a rendered deploy config
# carries the account id, the D1 database id and the Vectorize index id. It is
# gitignored, but gitignore does not govern what Docker sends as build context.
wrangler.toml
deploy/cloudflare/wrangler.toml
**/wrangler.toml

# Runtime secrets and local configuration. .env.example is safe and is not
# matched by these patterns; .env is not.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example

# Cloudflare local runtime state and the Worker test scratch directory.
.wrangler/
.workerd-temp/
**/.workerd-temp/

# The Worker is deployed by wrangler from its own directory, not baked into the
# Go backend image. Its node_modules is large and irrelevant here.
deploy/cloudflare/worker/node_modules/

# Version control and editor state.
.git/
.gitattributes
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
**/.DS_Store

# Test fixtures and evidence that are large and not needed to compile.
**/*_test.go
tests/fixtures/
mydocs/
ops/

# Local build output and coverage.
**/*.exe
**/*.test
**/coverage.out
go-service/archive-center-go
go-service/archive-center-updater
